user_prompt:
Enrich the canonical remittance facts with trading-partner, payer, payee, and rendering-policy context required to generate a valid, importable 835 when the free-text EOB is incomplete. This is the EOB workflow's equivalent of a context/enrichment stage. Do NOT modify any remit_canonical_package.semantic.* values — only add context and completion rules alongside them.

Resolve payee (priority order): (1) caller_context.practice_id/payee_id if given — treat as an explicit match; (2) exact match on a division/payee name extracted in remit_canonical_package; (3) lockbox# mapping if present; (4) fuzzy name match only if reasonably confident. If unresolved, set payee_context.source="none" and add missing_inputs: "Payee identity (practice_id or NPI/TIN) required".

Resolve payer (priority order): (1) caller_context.payer_id if given; (2) exact match on payer name/id extracted in remit_canonical_package; (3) fuzzy match on payer name candidates; (4) if only a portal/bank name exists (e.g. "J.P. Morgan") with no payer label context, do not treat it as payer and add warning PAYER_NOT_PRESENT_IN_TEXT. If unresolved, set payer_context.source="none" and add missing_inputs: "Payer identity required (payer_id or payer name)".

Build the x12_profile from caller_context (trading_partner_id, destination_profile_id) when supplied; otherwise use the default_v1 profile shown in the schema below (005010X221A1, delimiters * ~ :, sender MEDIKODE, usage_indicator P) and add warning DEFAULT_PROFILE_USED.

Construct completion_policy deterministically, at minimum covering: (A) DTM*405 payment date — use semantic.header.payment.payment_date if present else ingest.received_at date; (B) TRN02 — use trace_number if present, else check_number, else a synthetic id reproducible as "MK" + first_12(sha256_raw_text); (C) required payer/payee loops per rendering profile — never fabricate names, emit missing_inputs instead; (D) qualifier preferences for payer_id and payee_tin; (E) how unmapped_text[] is carried into X12 — prefer NTE segments, 80 chars max each.

For every enriched field, append a provenance.enriched_fields entry with path, source, confidence, and notes.

Validations: (V1) never change any remit_canonical_package semantic.* value; (V2) x12_profile.implementation_version, delimiters, and ISA/GS identifiers must be non-empty; (V3) below-threshold fuzzy matches must not be auto-selected — add missing_input and warning LOW_CONFIDENCE_MATCH instead; (V4) any synthetic identifier must be reproducible from sha256_raw_text.

Return ONLY this JSON object (no markdown, no extra text):
{
  "document_id": "doc_...",
  "package_type": "remit_context_package",
  "package_version": "1.0.0",
  "x12_profile": {
    "implementation_version": "005010X221A1",
    "delimiters": {
      "element": "*",
      "segment": "~",
      "component": ":"
    },
    "isa": {
      "sender_qual": "ZZ",
      "sender_id": "MEDIKODE",
      "receiver_qual": "ZZ",
      "receiver_id": "DESTSYS",
      "usage_indicator": "P"
    },
    "gs": {
      "functional_id": "HP",
      "sender_code": "MEDIKODE",
      "receiver_code": "DESTSYS"
    },
    "control_numbers": {
      "isa_control_policy": "sequential",
      "gs_control_policy": "sequential",
      "st_control_policy": "sequential",
      "starting_values": {
        "isa": 1,
        "gs": 1,
        "st": 1
      }
    },
    "required_loops": {
      "include_1000A": true,
      "include_1000B": true,
      "include_2000": true
    }
  },
  "payer_context": {
    "payer_id": "",
    "name": "",
    "id": "",
    "id_qualifier": "",
    "address": {
      "line1": "",
      "city": "",
      "state": "",
      "zip": ""
    },
    "match": {
      "method": "explicit|exact|fuzzy|none",
      "confidence": 0.0,
      "candidates": []
    },
    "source": "caller_context|payer_master|text|none"
  },
  "payee_context": {
    "payee_id": "",
    "name": "",
    "npi": "",
    "tin": "",
    "tin_qualifier": "TJ",
    "address": {
      "line1": "",
      "city": "",
      "state": "",
      "zip": ""
    },
    "match": {
      "method": "explicit|exact|fuzzy|none",
      "confidence": 0.0,
      "candidates": []
    },
    "source": "caller_context|payee_master|text|none"
  },
  "completion_policy": {
    "policy_id": "default_835_completion_v1",
    "policy_version": "1.0.0",
    "rules": [
      {
        "field": "DTM*405",
        "rule": "use semantic.header.payment.payment_date else ingest.received_at",
        "severity_if_missing": "warn"
      },
      {
        "field": "TRN02",
        "rule": "use check_number if present else generate trace id",
        "severity_if_missing": "warn"
      },
      {
        "field": "NTE",
        "rule": "preserve unmapped_text as NTE segments, max 80 chars each",
        "severity_if_missing": "none"
      }
    ],
    "qualifier_preferences": {
      "payer_id": [
        "XV",
        "PI",
        "XX"
      ],
      "payee_tin": [
        "TJ",
        "EI"
      ]
    }
  },
  "provenance": {
    "enriched_fields": [
      {
        "path": "payer_context.payer_id",
        "source": "payer_master",
        "confidence": 0.95,
        "notes": "matched payer by normalized name"
      }
    ]
  },
  "missing_inputs": [],
  "warnings": [],
  "errors": []
}

